{"text": "ALEXIS\n\nrofile.com\n\nemail@gmail.com - 123-456-7890 -\n\nExperience\nLocal Convention Centre September 2017 - present\nMeeting Manager\nT'manage the logistical and food & beverage elements of the meetings and special events markets.\n\u2018+ Manage all aspects of assigned meetings, conferences, and special events of up to 2,000\nattendees, while complying with internal requirements and aligning with Centre's business\npractices.\n\u2018+ Provide room setup and move-in /out suggestions to clients to ensure a successful event &\nmaintain fire code regulations.\n\u2018+ Suggest catering menus & additional services within clients\u2019 budgets that will enhance their\nevent.\n\u2018+ Work with clients to ensure event details are gathered in a timely manner and reflect company\u2019s\nbest practices.\n\u2018+ Effectively manage communication of event details to internal and external business partners,\nvendors, and suppliers.\n\u2018+ Utilize relationship management skills to troubleshoot any unique requests or onsite concerns\nfrom clients.\nObtain post-event feedback and evaluations from clients.\nEnsure invoices are accurate and provided to clients by the service standard timeline.\nProvide accurate and timely food & beverage revenue forecasting for all events assigned.\n\nLocal Convention Centre June 2016 - September 2017\nEvent Coordinator\ncoordinated the logistical elements of the conventions, tradeshows and meetings that take place.\n\u2018+ Planned logistical and food & beverage details for internal & external meetings.\n\u2018+ Answered general public & client inquiries about facility via verbal and written\ncommunication. Identified and escalated any concerns to appropriate managers or\ndepartments.\nLead site visits of the facility for clients.\nOn-site venue contact for clients during their event to ensure their on-site requests were\nactioned immediately.\n\u2018+ Provided training and guidance to new staff members and co-op students.\nSupported two event managers and a meeting manager.\nWorked within a team to implement changes to the Centre's Operating Guidelines across the\norganization. Organized a 4-day training for staff members on the Operating Guidelines.\n\nInternational Documentary Film Festival February - May 2016\nEvents Associate\nPart of a small team that coordinated 60+ events, leading up to and during the Festival,\n* Lead planner on 4 events.\n\u2018+ Trained and managed event volunteers.\n\u2018+ Assisted with maintaining key sponsor & industry relationships.",
